# serializer version: 1
# name: TestOnboarding.test_onboarding_dm_copy
  '''
  Set up PostHog - self-driving for your product
  
  ---
  
  👋 *Hi, I'm PostHog - self-driving for your product*
  I'm an AI agent on autopilot: I watch your product for problems, investigate them myself, and open pull requests to fix them - so issues get handled before they reach your backlog.
  
  💬 *You can also just talk to me*
  Tag `@PostHog` in any channel, or message me here, to dig into your product data or open a pull request. Name a project to route one question: `@PostHog give me DAU for Staging please`. `/posthog` lists my commands.
  
  ---
  
  *1. Connect your codebase* :wrench:
  Connect GitHub so I can fix things, not just flag them - when I spot a problem in your product I'll proactively open a pull request with the fix for you to review.
  
  [Connect GitHub](http://localhost:8010/integrations/connect/github/?project_id=<team_id>&connect_from=slack)
  
  *2. Choose what I watch* :eyes:
  Tick the signals I should monitor and investigate.
  
  [ ] *Error tracking*: new, reopened & spiking issues
  
  *3. Where I report* :inbox_tray:
  Everything I find lands in one shared channel so the team stays in the loop.
  
  [Create #posthog-inbox](slack_inbox_create)
  
  🎉 Once you're set up, I'll start watching your product and send your first report to #posthog-inbox as soon as I spot something.
  
  👍 Hit the thumbs under my replies when I get something wrong. Your default model and linked accounts live in my Home tab.
  '''
# ---
